The '''Port of Payra''' is a [[seaport]] located at [[Kalapara]] in [[Patuakhali]], [[Bangladesh]]. It was established by an [[Act of Parliament]] in 2013. The port was officially inaugurated in 2016. It is located on the Ramnabad Channel near the [[Bay of Bengal]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=15 August 2016|title=Bangladeshi Payra Port Inaugurated|url=http://worldmaritimenews.com/archives/199597/bangladeshi-payra-port-inaugurated/|publisher=Offshore Energy}}</ref> The port is undergoing several Development and expansion and the project is expected to be completed in 202.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Al Amin |first1=Mehedi |title=Slow but steady progress in Payra Port construction |url=https://www.dhakatribune.com/bangladesh/development/2019/02/16/slow-but-steady-progress-in-payra-port-construction |work=Dhaka Tribune |date=16 February 2019 |access-date=26 December 2020}}</ref>
==Development==
The development works include capital dredging of the port, the inauguration of eight ships, the first terminal, and the construction of a six-lane approach road and a bridge
===Capital Dredging===
The Payra Port Authority (PPA)  signed a deal with [[Belgium]]-based dredging company [[Jan De Nul]] (JDN) for capital and maintenance dredging of 75 kilometre long main channel of the under construction Payra seaport. March 2023 JAN DE NUL COMPLETES CAPITAL DREDGING IN PAYRA PORT .Now Port Access Channel was declared open for commercial <big>'vessels up to a draught of 10.5 m'</big>.Country's foreign currency Fund will be used for the dredging work under the [[Bangladesh Infrastructure Development Fund]]

Maintenance dredging will keep Payra Port accessible
Jan De Nul will perform the maintenance dredging of the port in the next phase of the project. Three Trailing Suction Hopper Dredgers will be deployed to the Rabnabad Channel of Payra Port to fulfil the dredging requirements of the coming years.<ref>{{Cite web |title=PM to open several development projects at Payra Seaport tomorrow |url=https://thefinancialexpress.com.bd/national/pm-to-open-several-development-projects-at-payra-seaport-tomorrow-1666762091 |access-date=2023-04-01 |website=The Financial Express |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Jan De Nul completes capital dredging in Payra Port |url=https://www.jandenul.com/news/jan-de-nul-completes-capital-dredging-payra-port |access-date=2023-04-01 |website=Jan De Nul |language=en}}</ref>
==Background==
Payra port was originally planned as [[China]]'s bid for another [[Deep-sea port|deep seaport]] in its [[String of Pearls (Indian Ocean)|String of Pearls]] strategy. The construction of the port, which was being financed on a public-private partnership (PPP) platform, was therefore granted to a Chinese company. [[India]], [[Japan]], and the [[United States]] opposed the plan.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Shepard |first=Wade |title=Bangladesh’s Deep Sea Port Problem |url=https://thediplomat.com/2016/06/bangladeshs-deep-sea-port-problem/ |access-date=2022-03-20 |website=thediplomat.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

In 2016, Indian companies stepped in to invest in the port.<ref name=":0" /> An MoU was signed with [[Jan De Nul|Jan De Nul Group]] in 2016 to dredge the Ramnabad canal.<ref>{{Cite web|date=14 June 2021|title=Major contract for Payra Port’s next dredging phase awarded to Jan De Nul|url=https://www.jandenul.com/news/major-contract-payra-ports-next-dredging-phase-awarded-jan-de-nul|access-date=2022-02-03|website=Jan De Nul}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Ganic|first=Eldin|date=2021-06-14|title=Jan De Nul signs Rabnabad dredging deal|url=https://www.offshore-energy.biz/jan-de-nul-signs-rabnabad-dredging-deal/|access-date=2022-02-03|website=Offshore Energy|language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=Khan |first=Sharier |last2=Noman |first2=Morshed |date=2021-04-19 |title=Payra downgraded to seaport from deep seaport |url=https://www.tbsnews.net/bangladesh/infrastructure/payra-downgraded-seaport-deep-seaport-234118 |access-date=2022-02-03 |website=The Business Standard |language=en}}</ref>  

As of 2017, Payra was primarily a governmental route for import and export.<ref>{{cite news |script-title=bn:নতুন পায়রা সমুদ্রবন্দর বাংলাদেশের জন্য কতটা গুরুত্বপূর্ণ |trans-title=The importance of the new Payra seaport |url=http://www.bbc.com/bengali/news/2015/10/151030_bd_paira_port |language=bn |work=BBC Bangla |date=30 October 2015 |access-date=2016-11-17}}</ref>

The [[Payra Port Authority]] is an autonomous agency which is responsible for the management of the seaport of Payra.<ref>{{cite news|date=30 November 2013|title=উদ্বোধন হলেও সচল হয়নি পায়রা বন্দর|script-title=|language=bn|trans-title=Port was not opened even after its inauguration|newspaper=Prothom Alo|url=http://www.prothom-alo.com/bangladesh/article/86317/%E0%A6%89%E0%A6%A6%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AC%E0%A7%8B%E0%A6%A7%E0%A6%A8-%E0%A6%B9%E0%A6%B2%E0%A7%87%E0%A6%93-%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%B2-%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%9F%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BF-%E0%A6%AA%E0%A6%BE%E0%A7%9F%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BE-%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A6%E0%A6%B0|url-status=dead|access-date=2016-11-17|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171223121048/http://www.prothom-alo.com:80/bangladesh/article/86317/%E0%A6%89%E0%A6%A6%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AC%E0%A7%8B%E0%A6%A7%E0%A6%A8-%E0%A6%B9%E0%A6%B2%E0%A7%87%E0%A6%93-%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%B2-%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%9F%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BF-%E0%A6%AA%E0%A6%BE%E0%A7%9F%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BE-%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A6%E0%A6%B0|archive-date=23 December 2017}}</ref>

As of 2021, plans to for a deep seaport at Payra have been shelved and the port was to be developed as a regular seaport.<ref name=":1" />

